Software Solution Architecture & Build Document
Chrome Extension Based Google Voice to CRM Call Tracking System
1. Purpose
This document defines the complete technical architecture, build story, and task breakdown for an
internal Chrome Extension that integrates Google Voice with the organization’s CRM to track calls,
duration, and transcripts.
2. Business Problem
Google Voice does not expose public APIs for call tracking. CRM users lack visibility into call
duration, transcripts, and outcomes, leading to manual logging and poor analytics.
3. Solution Overview
The system introduces a Chrome Extension that enables click-to-call from CRM, opens Google
Voice with a prefilled number, detects call lifecycle events, captures audio with consent, transcribes
calls, and stores results in CRM.
4. Architecture Components
• CRM Frontend (Call button, call status UI)
• Chrome Extension (MV3 background worker, content scripts)
• Google Voice Web UI (browser-based only)
• Speech-to-Text Service (Whisper or cloud STT)
• CRM Backend APIs
5. Call Flow
1. User clicks Call in CRM
2. Extension opens Google Voice with number
3. Call start detected via DOM observation
4. Timer and audio capture begin
5. Audio streamed to STT service
6. Transcript returned and stored
7. Call end detected and finalized
6. Data Model
Call records include user ID, contact ID, phone number, start/end time, duration, transcript, consent
flag, and timestamps
7. Permissions & Security
Chrome permissions include tabs, scripting, storage, and tabCapture. Consent is mandatory before
recording. All data must be transmitted securely over HTTPS.
8. Compliance
Explicit recording consent is required. Consent must be logged per call. Recording indicators must
be visible. Two-party consent laws must be respected.
9. Build Phases
Phase 0: Proof of Concept
Phase 1: MVP Call Logging
Phase 2: Transcription Integration
Phase 3: Hardening & Admin Controls
10. Limitations
• No official Google Voice APIs
• Approximate call duration
• Browser-only solution
• UI changes may require maintenance
11. Final Verdict
This is a technically feasible, cost-effective internal solution suitable for CRM visibility and analytics,
but not for carrier-grade compliance or billing use cases